            <ArticleTitle>A survey of 100 patients who had laparoscopic ventrosuspensions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>468-71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The technique for and results of 100 laparoscopic ventrosuspensions are described; patients were followed for an average of 40 months and in all but 11 the uterus was anteverted at the end of the follow-up period. The presenting symptoms of dyspareunia, dysmenorrhoea or sacral backache were almost always improved as a result of the operation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
